# Playwright constitution

Short standard for every task. Detail lives in `.cursor/rules/playwright-conventions.mdc`.

## MUST

| Rule | How |
| --- | --- |
| Role-based locators | `getByRole`, then `getByLabel` / `getByPlaceholder`, then `getByText`, then `getByTestId` with a comment; disambiguate with `.filter({ hasText })` |
| Web-first assertions | Retrying `expect(locator).toBeVisible()` / `.toBeEnabled()` / `.toHaveText()` in the spec |
| storageState auth | Feature tests start from the setup project's `playwright/.auth/user.json`; a login test clears that state and signs in through `LoginPage` |
| Unique self-cleaning data | Unique names; import `test` from `fixtures/cleanup.fixture.ts` and call `trackProgram(uuid)` as soon as the record exists |
| One tag per test | Exactly one of `@smoke`, `@sanity`, `@regression`, `@api`, `@e2e`, `@destructive` on each `test()`. `@destructive` only when the test changes locale, roles, flags, or settings, with an `afterEach` or `afterAll` that restores them. A test that only cleans up its own data keeps its importance tag |

## SHOULD

| Rule | How |
| --- | --- |
| Faker factories | Happy-path data comes from a factory under `test-data/factories`. Invalid values stay in a static `.ts` file. Secrets and URLs come from `process.env` |
| Enums for repeated strings | Put a string used in more than one file in an enum |
| JSDoc on action methods | Document each page-object action with a one-line JSDoc |

## WON'T

| Refuse | Stop because |
| --- | --- |
| XPath | A DOM-order locator clicks the wrong control after a restyle |
| `waitForTimeout` | A fixed sleep races the clock |
| Hardcoded secrets | A credential in source leaks into git |
| The `any` type | It hides the shape the assertion depends on |
| Weakened assertions | Dropping or softening an `expect` makes a failure look green |
| Healing a real bug | A defect triage classified as an app bug is filed; the locator stays |
| Tags on `describe` | A tag belongs on the single `test`, so one test is one filter |

## Agent governance

Behavioral contract for every non-trivial task. Nothing in this section is hook-enforced.

A task is non-trivial when it edits files, picks a design, or depends on a name that is not already in the request.

### Audit, then edit

Read the files and conventions the change touches. Emit this block before any edit:

```
Proposal
- Scope: files and behavior this task will change
- Confidence: 1-10
- Rationale: why this scope and this score
- Unknowns: what is still unverified, or none
```

### Confidence gate

| Score | Do |
| --- | --- |
| below 5 | Stop. Ask for the missing input. Do not edit. |
| 5-7 | Proceed only with the unknowns listed and a human's approval |
| 8 or above | Proceed |

Never invent a path, enum, env var, credential, or message. Ask, or explore the repo, the ticket, and the environment, and use only a value that is already there.

